316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (Members of this bloc emphasize that Arctic development should remain primarily under the authority of the Arctic States. While they recognize the economic opportunities that come with foreign investments, they are wary of indirect control and exploitation of their regions. They would favor frameworks that allow Arctic governments to maintain strong regulatory oversight over infrastructure and natural resources. States within this bloc often support sustainable development policies in accordance with their Indigenous communities. However, disputes may arise on the degree of openness toward foreign investors as well as the scale of development projects.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
